Leave the 20 MP mode out: libcamera always picks the biggest one

The 5184x3880 mode WORKS. It is not withdrawn because it is broken, it is
withdrawn because libcamera always picks the highest-resolution mode and with it
declared the Plasma camera ends up unusable for two reasons at once:

SLOWNESS. libcamera's Bayer development runs on the CPU. Measured on the phone:

    Debayer processed 30 frames in 1604557us, 53485 us/frame

53 ms per frame is barely 19 per second, and the viewfinder stutters. At
2592x1940 it is four times fewer pixels.

DARKNESS. The 5 MP mode comes out of a 2x2 binning, that is four times more
light per pixel. With the same scene and the same exposure, the signal above the
black pedestal was ~6 times higher in the combined one:

    mode         median    (pedestal = 64)
    2592x1940      70..156
    5184x3880      65

So the big mode gives less image and costs four times the work.

WARNING FOR THE FUTURE
----------------------
An earlier version of this patch said the big mode "produces no image". IT WAS
FALSE, and the instrument was to blame: the analysis used 3240 bytes per line
(2592 packed pixels) when the real stride is 3248 -there are 8 bytes of padding-
so every row was shifted and the unpacking went out of alignment. It was
withdrawn before compiling. The mode is kept in the file, marked __maybe_unused,
to restore it when there is hardware development.
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@
 	{ CCI_REG16(0xb13c), 0x0800 },
 };
 
-static const struct cci_reg_sequence s5k3t2_mode_5184x3880[] = {
+static const struct cci_reg_sequence __maybe_unused s5k3t2_mode_5184x3880[] = {
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x6028), 0x4000 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x0136), 0x1300 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x013e), 0x00c8 },
@@ -620,17 +620,40 @@
 			.num_regs = ARRAY_SIZE(s5k3t2_mode_2592x1940),
 		},
 	},
-	{
-		.width = 5184,
-		.height = 3880,
-		.hts = 5440,
-		.vts = 4160,
-		.exposure = 512,
-		.reg_list = {
-			.regs = s5k3t2_mode_5184x3880,
-			.num_regs = ARRAY_SIZE(s5k3t2_mode_5184x3880),
-		},
-	},
+	/*
